{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>20</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">One of the two equations in a system of linear equations is given. The system has exactly one solution. Which equation could be the second equation in the system?</p>", "keys": ["b545b92f-e975-48e0-92b9-2d1d156093e1"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "b000e6cf-b31f-4494-9bb0-f9a71e9f0d87", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"3 x plus 3 y equals 60\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>60</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "9871f466-cd76-4df6-9451-5f4beb37388b", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"negative x minus y equals 40\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>40</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "1a5e7b32-58d5-4915-b2e5-7c48e07a6a1b", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"3 x plus 3 y equals 14\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>14</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "b545b92f-e975-48e0-92b9-2d1d156093e1", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"x minus y equals 20\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>20</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. A system of two linear equations in two variables, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>, has exactly one solution if the graphs of the lines represented by the equations in the <em>xy</em>-plane have different slopes. In the <em>xy</em>-plane, the slope of a line defined by an equation in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A x plus upper B y equals upper C\"><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi></math> are constants, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus StartFraction upper A Over upper B EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></math>. It&rsquo;s given that one equation in the system is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>. It follows that for this equation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 1\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B equals 1\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus StartFraction upper A Over upper B EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative one oneth\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 1\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. For the equation in choice D, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x minus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 1\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper B equals negative 1\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus StartFraction upper A Over upper B EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus StartFraction 1 Over left parenthesis negative 1 right parenthesis EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Since the slopes are different, it follows that the system of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x minus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math> has exactly one solution. Thus, the second equation in the system could be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x minus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. The equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 x plus 3 y equals 60\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math> can be rewritten as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math> is the same as the given equation, the system of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 x plus 3 y equals 60\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math> has infinitely many solutions rather than exactly one solution.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. The equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative x minus y equals 40\"><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></math> can be rewritten as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals negative 40\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></math>. The graph of this line has a slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 1\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Since the graphs of the lines represented by the equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals negative 40\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math> have the same slope in the <em>xy</em>-plane and the equations aren't equivalent, this system has no solution rather than exactly one solution.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. The equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 x plus 3 y equals 14\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math> can be rewritten as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals StartFraction 14 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. The graph of this line has a slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 1\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Since the graphs of the lines represented by the equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals StartFraction 14 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x plus y equals 20\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math> have the same slope in the <em>xy</em>-plane and the equations aren't equivalent, this system has no solution rather than exactly one solution.</p>", "externalid": "35175215-d90c-49a0-927c-7f816dae6a5d", "correct_answer": ["D"]}